From a4e841fb82c8e8d24e83b352365593bb1574e11f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:40:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse unroutable classes before claiming
 [daveey]

Problem: an eligible class peer was held by a second raw legacy-pin quota probe; unroutable classes were claimed and fell back through profile routing.
Why: neutral quota preflight fell through to retired executable selectors, and class validity was only checked after claim. Remove the raw probe and refuse proven-unroutable classes at preclaim. Existing quota episodes retain their typed deadline ownership.

Proof: raw live-wall regression fails at missing legacy card launch before repair, four invalid registries fail with real launches. Canonical retries-disabled final 12-file group: 287 passed, one failure retained. Original eleven residual nodes pass, including zero-claim/run unroutable/quota/pacing controls and typed unknown-author refusal. New integration regression in repeated review refusal escapes from generic class preflight before existing review escalation; preserved for bounded next disposition, NOT review/landing ready. No fleet mutations, author exclusion changes, pins or quota bypass.
